  "claims": {
    "checked_analysis_invariance": "Computed input dependencies, required operation IDs and fresh operation obligations are invariant along EVERY checked Exchange path, including its existing prefix/suffix contexts.",
    "repair_transport": "Existing local kernel equality proofs transport across the checked order; the repair/reorder square compares the actual projected execution laws from one common initial store.",
    "bounded_higher_forms": "Three explicit schematic higher generator forms: swap involution, three-box braid, disjoint two-pair exchange. Their core words have 2, 3 and 4 operation occurrences; primitive-swap counts on their boundary paths are 2/0, 3/3 and 2/2. No arbitrary-parallel-path or global-normalization generator.",
    "higher_scope": "The newly DEFINED higher relation has reflexivity, reversal, transitivity, path-composition and surrounding-context closures. Global coherence/completeness, path groupoid law completion, repeated-ID/self-exchange analysis and heterogeneous/copy/discard completion remain unproved.",
    "negative_boundary": "Two constant-overwrite boxes give equal full old execution laws in opposite orders but different required/fresh sets. Updating only operation false makes their observed final Boolean false versus true. Mere old semantic equivalence is not stable under kernel edits.",
    "source_checker_still_sound": "The original-order projected marginal is preserved by that edit and its dataflow-only reuse check correctly accepts; this does not license reusing the old reordering proof.",
    "proof_support": "An imported old equivalence receives a conservative support equal to the UNION of the two endpoint required sets. Matching new kernels on this set suffices to transport the old equivalence. Checked Exchange certificates are uniform in all kernels and therefore need no kernel-equality support, while static interfaces and guards remain required.",
    "certificate_composition": "ReusePlan stores pure executable metadata; ReuseCertificate adds an explicitly checked old validity proof. Supports combine by union through composition and are preserved by reversal. Fresh support is its intersection with changed operation IDs.",
    "executable_checker": "The metadata-only plan checker runs without evaluating noncomputable PMF semantics. Acceptance plus unchanged-operation proofs implies updated equivalence. Rejection requests new sufficient conditions, not a general impossibility result."
  },
