  "scope": [
    "Same enforced read/write interfaces across kernel updates.",
    "Fixed finite operation schedules, with arbitrary data-dependent actions and discrete PMFs as before.",
    "Exact observed-law equalities, not general approximate cryptographic reductions.",
    "Imported equivalences are supplied Lean proofs; they are NOT primitive polygraph equations or automatically solved semantic equalities.",
    "Computed supports are sufficient and conservative, not minimal dependency sets.",
    "New examples are diagnostic; no new nontrivial query reordering of the actual MAC caller is claimed. The previous full MAC refinement and cache/trace exchange rejection remain unchanged.",
    "Higher forms are explicit proof data, but global higher coherence is not proved.",
    "No new native runtime, proof DAG-size, kernel-byte or proof-checking-time bound."
  ],
  "research_consequence": "Do not compare proof-repair obligations solely as invariants of the game distribution. Track the support of the proof transformation and require stability under the edited semantics.",
